{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler/stitch pipeline task #5126. The task requires creating differential tests for `cmd/true` utility in file `cmd/true/true_test.go`. Specifically:\n   - Write TestDiff using `testutils.BuildBinary` and `testutils.RunDiffTests` to compare against `gtrue` (srd013-true R3.1)\n   - Skip test gracefully if `gtrue` reference binary is not found via `exec.LookPath` (srd013-true R3.2)\n   - Test no-argument invocation exits 0 with empty stdout and stderr (srd013-true R4.1)\n   - Test `--help` and `--version` flags produce matching output (srd013-true R4.2)\n   - Test that arbitrary arguments are silently ignored with exit 0 (srd013-true R4.3)\n   \n   Acceptance criteria: `go test ./cmd/true/... -count=1` passes (or skips if gtrue not installed), follows RunDiffTests pattern, at least 3 test cases (no args, --help, --version), `go vet ./cmd/true/` passes.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary (gtrue from Homebrew coreutils)\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles the cmd/ package and returns binary path\n   - `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` runs side-by-side comparison\n   - `DiffTest` struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   - Graceful skip pattern: `exec.LookPath(\"gtrue\")` + `t.Skip` if not found\n   - LC_ALL=C set by default in the harness\n   - SIGPIPE handler pattern required for cmd/ utilities\n   - Copyright header required on all Go files\n   - Git is managed externally - NO git commands allowed\n   - Constitution requires: functions ≤40 lines, files ≤500 lines, no scope creep\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd013-true.yaml` (READ)\n     - Defines all requirements for `true` utility\n     - R1: Core behavior (exit 0, ignore args, no output)\n     - R2: Help/version output (--help prints usage, --version prints version, write error exits 1)\n     - R3: Exit codes (only 0 or 1)\n     - R4: Differential testing requirements (compare exit codes, cover no-args/arbitrary-args/--help/--version)\n   \n   - `cmd/true/main.go` (READ - existing implementation)\n     - Already implemented with SIGPIPE handler, --help, --version support\n     - Key code:\n     ```go\n     package main\n     import (\n         \"fmt\"\n         \"os\"\n         \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n     )\n     const helpText = `Usage: true [ignored command line arguments]\n       or:  true OPTION\n     Exit with a status code indicating success.\n           --help     display this help and exit\n           --version  output version information and exit\n     `\n     const versionText = `true (go-unix-utils) dev\n     `\n     func main() {\n         sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n         if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n             switch os.Args[1] {\n             case \"--help\":\n                 if _, err := fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText); err != nil {\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n                 return\n             case \"--version\":\n                 if _, err := fmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText); err != nil {\n                     os.Exit(1)\n                 }\n                 return\n             }\n         }\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (READ - testing harness)\n     - `DiffTest` struct definition with all fields\n     - `RunDiffTests` iterates test cases, runs both binaries, compares outputs\n     - `buildEnv` merges test env with process env, sets LC_ALL=C\n     - `compareOutputs` does byte-equal comparison on stdout, stderr, and exit code\n     - `TimestampNormalizer` and `ComposeNormalizers` available for output normalization\n\n   - `pkg/testutils/build.go` (READ - binary builder)\n     - `BuildBinary(t, dir)` compiles Go package at dir, returns path to binary in temp dir\n     ```go\n     func BuildBinary(t *testing.T, dir string) string {\n         t.Helper()\n         name := resolvePackageName(dir)\n         tmpDir := t.TempDir()\n         binPath := filepath.Join(tmpDir, name)\n         cmd := exec.Command(\"go\", \"build\", \"-o\", binPath, dir)\n         output, err := cmd.CombinedOutput()\n         if err != nil {\n             t.Fatalf(\"BuildBinary: go build %s failed: %v\\n%s\", dir, err, output)\n         }\n         return binPath\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - `cmd/true/true_test.go` (TO BE CREATED)\n     - This is the file that needs to be written\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet - the task was interrupted before any code was written.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Gathered all necessary information: SRD requirements, existing implementation, testutils API, and established patterns\n   - Identified potential issue: `--help` and `--version` output from Go binary (\"true (go-unix-utils) dev\") won't match GNU gtrue output. Differential tests for these will fail when gtrue is present. But the task requires testing them, so they should be included.\n   - The test will gracefully skip when gtrue is not installed, so CI won't break.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The single user message contains the entire task specification including: role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, execution constitution, go style constitution, shared protocols, and package contracts. The core request is to implement task #5126: create `cmd/true/true_test.go` with differential tests.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/true/true_test.go` with differential tests\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/true/` to verify no warnings\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/true/... -count=1` to verify tests pass (or skip)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all four required files (SRD, main.go, difftest.go, build.go) and was about to create `cmd/true/true_test.go`. The file needs to follow the differential testing pattern from the shared_protocols:\n   ```go\n   func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n       goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n       refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gtrue\")\n       if err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\") }\n       tests := []testutils.DiffTest{ ... }\n       testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n   }\n   ```\n   \n   Test cases needed:\n   - No args: `{Name: \"no-args\", ExitCode: 0}` - verifies exit 0, no output\n   - With --help: `{Name: \"help\", Args: []string{\"--help\"}, ExitCode: 0}`\n   - With --version: `{Name: \"version\", Args: []string{\"--version\"}, ExitCode: 0}`\n   - Arbitrary args ignored: `{Name: \"arbitrary-args\", Args: []string{\"foo\", \"bar\", \"--baz\"}, ExitCode: 0}`\n\n   The file needs: copyright header, package main, imports (testing, os/exec, testutils package).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/true/true_test.go` with the complete test implementation, then run `go vet ./cmd/true/` and `go test ./cmd/true/... -count=1` to verify acceptance criteria. The task description states: \"Implement — Complete the work described in Requirements and Files to Create/Modify\" and the file to create is `cmd/true/true_test.go` with action \"create\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5126/5badfbfd-bac2-4647-9777-646ed13c33ae.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do no